{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1413503-what-is-life-like-for-a-mortal-raised-in-yu-shan-as-a-sidereal-agent","id":1413503,"title":"What is life like for a MORTAL raised in Yu-Shan? As a Sidereal Agent?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-14T00:54:06-07:00","id":1413503,"title":"What is life like for a MORTAL raised in Yu-Shan? As a Sidereal Agent?","content":"Imagine a dragonblood taken at birth and raised in Yu-Shan to be an operative directly for an individual (unconventional) Sidereal <i>or</i> the Bureau of Fate as a whole. The purpose is to make a loyal dragonblood agent who can do and knows about things a DB used as an unwitting tool doesn't. What would this individual's life be like? What kind of training would they receive? How would you guess the Sidereals would treat or handle them? Loyal pet? Professional and distant - like a low level employee? Or would some dote on him? Care about him?<br /> <br /> Before you say &quot;there are better ways to do that&quot; - I appreciate that. This is something my player wanted, and I liked the idea a lot, so I'm definitely doing it. I need help making it believable as is and some ideas what I should probably know about the Bureau or Yu-Shan (I'm vaguely familiar but I never read the 2e Sidereal or Heaven books).<br /> <br /> I appreciate any help you folks can give me!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4407,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4407-loving-the-gorgon","user":"Loving the Gorgon","date":". 09-14-2020, 04:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4407-loving-the-gorgon","name":"Loving the Gorgon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4407_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-14T01:14:43-07:00","id":1413508,"title":"","content":"This is totally a thing! It's covered in Heirs (sorry, I feel like that's pretty much all I talk about on here) in a section called Heaven's Dragons. Basically, some DB survivors of the Divine Revolution who entered Heaven never left and have carved out impressive estates for themselves amidst Yu-Shan's forsaken areas/slums. They're often engaged as fixers or troubleshooters by Gods and Sidereals, able to do 'off the books' stuff (black market trade/spy missions in Creation, that kind of thing) that others can't touch. I've spoilered a couple of paras that might be helpful from the rest of the entry if of use:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded are largely exempt from the bureaucratic regulations governing both gods and Sidereals, and use this freedom to fill gaps in the Celestial Bureaucracy left by years of internal rivalry, corruption, and divine disinterest. Their Exalted might levels the playing field when competing against minor gods and functionary spirits for positions as retainers, spies, professional confidants, bodyguards, and advisors. This novelty also makes them popular as entertainers and artisans \u2014 even if a novice Dragon-Blood\u2019s technique falls short of that of an ancient god of art, she brings a unique life experience and perspective that tantalizes divine audiences. Some pursue other skilled trades: personal accountants, bankers, artificers, assassins, and the like.<br /> <br /> ON ASSIGNMENT<br /> <br /> Most gods who reside Yu-Shan have little desire to abandon its sublime luxuries to walk Creation on errands. Even among those willing to do so, not all can easily afford a sabbatical from their position in the Celestial Bureaucracy, and some business is better conducted with the benefit of plausible deniability. Thus, Heaven\u2019s Dragons often find themselves retained to carry out the work of the gods in Creation. Travel to Creation is usually business-related, assigned to the Dragon-Blooded by her employer or family, though leaving Heaven out of personal curiosity or punitive banishment isn\u2019t unheard of.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 09-17-2020, 10:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-14T01:20:56-07:00","id":1413510,"title":"","content":"I think your player\u2019s character would be doted on by her Sidereal handler. Sort of like a loving but occasionally overly smothering parental figure. However, other Sidereals in the Bureau of Fate are likely to be more distant toward the PC and occasionally manipulate her for their own ends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-14T01:24:19-07:00","id":1413511,"title":"","content":"Dang, nice info ya'll! Thank you! Welcoming any other perspectives! I'm really glad to hear this is not just doable but very lore-friendly for my player <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4407-loving-the-gorgon","name":"Loving the Gorgon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4407_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-15T05:08:34-07:00","id":1413755,"title":"","content":"I think this is a very cool idea<br /> <br /> I'd expect the outward attitude of a sidereal to be partly dependent on their caste: a stereotypical chosen of venus would be doting bordering on smothering, a stereotypical chosen of battles a harsh but fair 'commanding officer' and a stereotypical chosen of secrets would give Gendo Ikari a run for his money in the bad father department.<br /> <br /> The theme of Sidereals is that they are spies and manipulators, so regardless of the outward appearance of the relationship, inwardly they are going to be torn between two things: the human tendency to love and protect those close to them, and their duty to protect creation and destiny even if it means sacrificing everyone and everything around them. I'd expect the big reveal of this story to be either &quot;Mom didn't love me even though she said she did&quot; or &quot;Mom really did love me even though she said she didn't&quot;<br /> <br /> The two big questions for me would be 1) how much of the DB's upbringing and life was a lie (could be a lot of it, the DB might not know they live in Heaven or what a Sidereal even is) or they could be openly told that they are an agent of Destiny - but either way the whole setup will be designed to maximise loyalty.<br /> <br /> The second question is: how many other similar agents does the Sidereal have, currently and in the past?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3174-carl-ollivier","name":"Carl.ollivier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-15T10:21:56-07:00","id":1413795,"title":"","content":"There's probably a big difference in the outlook of a mortal raised by a sidereal and one who's merely an unexalted scion of Yu Shan's native dragon blooded population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T06:19:56-07:00","id":1413953,"title":"","content":"Probably quite a different outlook on Creation.<br /> <br /> Most people in Creation? They're poor. They live in dirt huts, they eat rice with vegetables, and maybe some meat if they're lucky. And they probably die at 50. <br /> <br /> In Yu-shan? The streets are paved with jade. The gods themselves march by your side. Even the poorest god easily has riches that will match a mortal prince or a king. In Yu-shan, the food is Resources 4/5 on Creation, is supernaturally tasty, and makes you heal faster. The daily samples and foods you take in Yu-Shan is the kind of shit that can match the Manchu-Han Imperial Feast. Everyday. The finest silks, the most wonderful perfume, the softest shoes.... all of those are things that anyone with the slightest means in Yu-Shan can obtain. And there is far, far more. Celestial Wine, Divine lovers.... all those things are available, so long as you get the power. <br /> <br /> Now, if they're raised by a Sidereal in Yu-shan? Unless the Sidereal is some kind of weird ass ascetic, they're going to have all this. <br /> <br /> They might despise being sent out on missions, the same way I'll despise being sent out into the countryside with no working internet and having to poo in a hole in a ground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T13:57:27-07:00","id":1414037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1413503-what-is-life-like-for-a-mortal-raised-in-yu-shan-as-a-sidereal-agent?p=1413953#post1413953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably quite a different outlook on Creation.<br /> <br /> Most people in Creation? They're poor. They live in dirt huts, they eat rice with vegetables, and maybe some meat if they're lucky. And they probably die at 50. <br /> <br /> In Yu-shan? The streets are paved with jade. The gods themselves march by your side. Even the poorest god easily has riches that will match a mortal prince or a king. In Yu-shan, the food is Resources 4/5 on Creation, is supernaturally tasty, and makes you heal faster. The daily samples and foods you take in Yu-Shan is the kind of shit that can match the Manchu-Han Imperial Feast. Everyday. The finest silks, the most wonderful perfume, the softest shoes.... all of those are things that anyone with the slightest means in Yu-Shan can obtain. And there is far, far more. Celestial Wine, Divine lovers.... all those things are available, so long as you get the power. <br /> <br /> Now, if they're raised by a Sidereal in Yu-shan? Unless the Sidereal is some kind of weird ass ascetic, they're going to have all this. <br /> <br /> They might despise being sent out on missions, the same way I'll despise being sent out into the countryside with no working internet and having to poo in a hole in a ground.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s true. Yu-Shan is Heaven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T17:42:08-07:00","id":1414101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1413503-what-is-life-like-for-a-mortal-raised-in-yu-shan-as-a-sidereal-agent?p=1414037#post1414037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That\u2019s true. Yu-Shan is Heaven.</div> </div> </div> </div>And not to mention the casual excellence on display. <br /> <br /> Like, every god in Yu-shan has at least 3 dice in equipment bonuses, at least an excellency in something, and, if nothing else, has godliness and divine power to back up their strength in one or two things. Not to mention the greatest archive of information and knowledge in Creation. And that's not telling what happens if the Sidereal minder is a chosen of secrets. <br /> <br /> The dude going to a scholar convention and listening to people talk about science or the first age would be like a 21st century physicist going to the past and listening to people talk about ether and vitalism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T18:24:04-07:00","id":1414113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1413503-what-is-life-like-for-a-mortal-raised-in-yu-shan-as-a-sidereal-agent?p=1414101#post1414101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, every god in Yu-shan has at least 3 dice in equipment bonuses...</div> </div> </div> </div>Exceptional equipment in 3e only gives one bonus die, and not to combat rolls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The dude going to a scholar convention and listening to people talk about science or the first age would be like a 21st century physicist going to the past and listening to people talk about ether and vitalism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, imagine the vistas of knowledge that'd be opened by being able to question the ancients about the things they wrote down and why. Most of the documents we <i>do</i> have references material that's been lost forever. It'd be a singular learning experience.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T18:47:50-07:00","id":1414118,"title":"","content":"I've never been a fan of the 'wisdom of the ancients' trope. If they were that smart and powerful, where were their steam engines and antibiotics?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T19:10:01-07:00","id":1414122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1413503-what-is-life-like-for-a-mortal-raised-in-yu-shan-as-a-sidereal-agent?p=1414118#post1414118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never been a fan of the 'wisdom of the ancients' trope.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not talking about tropes. I'm talking about history. There's a lot we don't know about the past, about which we can only speculate. Even for ancient junk science, the ability to check the sources they're citing would show us a lot about the world they lived in.<br /> <br /> \u200b(Also antibiotics might not be the high-water mark of wisdom, considering how our misuse of it has led to antibiotic resistance being bred into a ridiculous quantity of bacteria.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 09-16-2020, 10:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T19:45:59-07:00","id":1414130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1413503-what-is-life-like-for-a-mortal-raised-in-yu-shan-as-a-sidereal-agent?p=1414122#post1414122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not talking about tropes. I'm talking about history. There's a lot we don't know about the past, about which we can only speculate. Even for ancient junk science, the ability to check the sources they're citing would show us a lot about the world they lived in.<br /> <br /> \u200b(Also antibiotics might not be the high-water mark of wisdom, considering how our misuse of it has led to antibiotic resistance being bred into a ridiculous quantity of bacteria.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh god, this again. <br /> <br /> Well, Antibiotics are the high water mark of wisdom, considering how many lives they've saved. I mean, a single infected cut can be the end of your life in the ancient world. And now? It isn't. <br /> <br /> Im not looking for the world they live in. I'm looking for shit that can be used to improve human lives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T21:43:06-07:00","id":1414135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1413503-what-is-life-like-for-a-mortal-raised-in-yu-shan-as-a-sidereal-agent?p=1414118#post1414118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never been a fan of the 'wisdom of the ancients' trope. If they were that smart and powerful, where were their steam engines and antibiotics?</div> </div> </div> </div>Antibiotics was literally discovered by accident, by a guy who wasn't even looking for it. Not exactly a super-genius moment in human history.<br /> <br /> Issac Newton tried to figure out the celestial mechanics of planetary orbits, with noting more than a pen, paper, and ancient telescope. Sadly the math to figure out the forces involved didn't exist. Luckily he was a <i>freaking genius</i> so he invented integral calculus over the course of a few weeks. It takes most people longer than that to learn integral calculus from a teacher who knows it well.<br /> <br /> Plato in 450BC basically came up with the idea for the film The Matrix, and the possibility that everything we experience is not reflective of the real world. We just don't know the difference because, of course, our senses can not detect the real world. Which is actually 100% true. We perceive things as solid and not as vast empty spaces with atomic nuclei in them because our senses do not give us that information.<br /> <br /> <br /> The reason ancients didn't have workable steam engines, among some other reasons, is because the tools and materials to create steam engines didn't exist. Well, actually primitive steam engines are over 2,000 years old, they had them, they just weren't large and didn't have the power to do useful work. For that you need a lot of steam, and a very large engine, you probably want steel, because copper, especially hot cooper, from a mechanical standpoint sucks in comparison, you want proper insulation, you need an understanding of fluid dynamics and thermodynamics to properly shape things, etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Here's the thing though. Only some of that applies to things like the philosophy of justice, or happiness, or what it means to be a good person. Let me hit you with some stuff:<br /> <br /> <b>Aristotle born 384 BC</b><br /> <br /> &quot;The life of money-making is one undertaken under compulsion, and wealth is evidently not the good we are seeking; for it is merely useful and for the sake of something else.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;It is the mark of an educated mind to be able to entertain a thought without accepting it.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Anyone can become angry, that is easy. To become angry with the correct person, in the correct degree, at the right time, and to achieve the right ends, that is not easy, and is not within everyone's power.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Laozi born 5th century BC</b><br /> <br /> &quot;Being deeply loved by someone gives you strength, and loving someone deeply gives you courage.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Mastering others is strength, but mastering yourself is real power.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Pericles born 495 BC</b><br /> <br /> &quot;What you leave behind is not what's engraved in stone monuments, but the changes you've made in the lives of the people you touched.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Seneca born 4 BC</b><br /> <br /> &quot;Anger is an acid that does more harm to the vessel that holds it than onto anything it is poured.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> That's good stuff, but honestly it's better read in full. There's lots of that in public domain that you can read free online. They talk about things like how to cope with inevitable death, the purpose and dangers of emotion, how to control that emotion, how to improve mental health. All sorts of things that have barely changed at all in thousands of years, things millions of people are struggling with at this very moment.<br /> <br /> It's at least worth considering that people who have pondered their whole lives on personal subjects like that, and who are quoted millenia after their deaths might have something interesting to talk about in person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T02:17:35-07:00","id":1414158,"title":"","content":"I'm fine with philosophical and mathematical insights. After all, those are near-universal to the human experience. <br /> <br /> Technology and science? No.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T05:02:04-07:00","id":1414176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1413503-what-is-life-like-for-a-mortal-raised-in-yu-shan-as-a-sidereal-agent?p=1414158#post1414158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm fine with philosophical and mathematical insights. After all, those are near-universal to the human experience. <br /> <br /> Technology and science? No.</div> </div> </div> </div>My boyfriend told me someone in the Roman Empire invented plastic but the Emperor put him to death so the new invention wouldn\u2019t destroy the metal industry. Plastic wasn\u2019t invented again until 1913. And I think they had concrete in Ancient Rome too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T05:25:26-07:00","id":1414181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1413503-what-is-life-like-for-a-mortal-raised-in-yu-shan-as-a-sidereal-agent?p=1414176#post1414176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My boyfriend told me someone in the Roman Empire invented plastic but the Emperor put him to death so the new invention wouldn\u2019t destroy the metal industry. Plastic wasn\u2019t invented again until 1913. And I think they had concrete in Ancient Rome too.</div> </div> </div> </div>They had concrete, yes. Plastic, a mere myth, I believe. <br /> <br /> Concrete yes. But they had their own issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T18:10:04-07:00","id":1414308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1413503-what-is-life-like-for-a-mortal-raised-in-yu-shan-as-a-sidereal-agent?p=1413953#post1413953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, if they're raised by a Sidereal in Yu-shan? Unless the Sidereal is some kind of weird ass ascetic, they're going to have all this.<br /> <br /> They might despise being sent out on missions, the same way I'll despise being sent out into the countryside with no working internet and having to poo in a hole in a ground.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, in Yu-Shan they probably exist entirely on a line of credit from the Sidereal and viewed as a lesser entity for it. <br /> A cursory glance at the history of womens rights shows us that living like this can be its own cage even if its a gilded one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T18:29:46-07:00","id":1414311,"title":"","content":"It's also about context. If all they've known is Heaven, they could very easily feel poor and indigent. They only get one measly feast a day. Their divinely woven robes are the same ones they wore last week.<br /> <br /> Kinda like people who grow up in a wealthy nation, and then travel. I'm by no means wealthy in America. But if you sent me to rural Burkina Faso with the Peace Corps, all of a sudden my normal life looks pretty luxurious. My apartment is private, climate controlled, and my electricity works all of the time. I can go be incredibly picky about fruits, vegetables, and meat and get them pretty much regardless of the season. I hardly ever need to bribe or talk my way past a military checkpoint, and my commute is both short, and by vehicle. And I have more reliable and fast internet access via this phone than can be believed. I can stream virtually any entertainment I want, with the push of a button. And when I stop to really think about it, I am, in many ways quite wealthy. But most days, I certainly don't feel that way. Because in America, I'm lower middle class, with a blue collar job, in a tiny studio apartment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader","name":"Scrollreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26421_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-17T18:30:09-07:00","id":1414312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1413503-what-is-life-like-for-a-mortal-raised-in-yu-shan-as-a-sidereal-agent?p=1414308#post1414308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, in Yu-Shan they probably exist entirely on a line of credit from the Sidereal and viewed as a lesser entity for it.<br /> A cursory glance at the history of womens rights shows us that living like this can be its own cage even if its a gilded one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... <br /> <br /> DB, right? <br /> <br /> In that case, who's to say that he doesn't have his own unofficial salary? I mean, greater spirits hire smaller ones to gather quintessence. Why not hire this DB who has his own powers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T12:01:29-07:00","id":1414433,"title":"","content":"I played a Mortal in Yu-Shan for some time in a game. He wasn't a DB raised as an agent, but rather a future Sidereal as a teenager whose safehouse became unsafe so he was relocated to Heaven with what amounted to full time bodyguards and protectors.<br /> <br /> His prior incarnation had life insurance which gave him money, but money and the way people treated him didn't do much to deal with his social anxiety. To him, it was like moving from the real world into a fairytale, and he was extremely uncomfortable with the sudden increase in luxury he obtained, while at the same time being able to see and observe and even speak to people who were even poorer or generally worse off then he had been living at a monastery. The rich were richer, but the poor were also poorer, and I think that's something to consider on both sides of the coin. Someone coming back to Creation from Yu-Shan to live there isn't going to be like 'what the fuck is a poor person?' or be like 'you rich people are peasants', unless they have a serious superiority complex that would cause issues with their work as an agent. I think their response is more likely to be a note in the change in amount but not the change in status; the rich are still rich, they still live in exorbitant mansions filled with workers and wear finery and do their high society things, and the poor are still poor, begging on street corners and doing menial jobs to try and make end's meet.<br /> <br /> I think even characters like that would be able to comprehend the observation that for all the differences in the trappings, the baseline societies between Yu-Shan and any generally advanced society in Creation- advanced enough to have dedicated societal roles and an upper and lower class- are not particularly different, when you're specifically training and educating someone for the express purpose of being integrated into a society directly, I think those people would be even more aware of such things and not be particularly freaked out about them.<br /> <br /> They might be receiving less luxury then they're used to in an absolute sense, but if you're training this person to be a specific agent, I can't see them not being able to deal with that, or not being aware of it. They may need a little bit to get used to it, missing out on some things that they might be used to without a substitute, but only in the same way that, say, I had to get used to missing one of my favorite restaurants when I moved; I still miss it and remember the meal I ordered and can taste it, but I don't get to have it anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T13:12:22-07:00","id":1414454,"title":"","content":"One thought I had is that the prices of different goods can vary dramatically. The amount of silver/year it takes to hire a full-time servant in Yu-Shan is probably a lot higher than in Creation, so I'd expect a rich person in Creation to have many more servants and less jewelry than a rich person in Yu-Shan. I could imagine someone from Yu-Shan visiting Creation thinking, simultaneously &quot;it's amazing that even the richest people here struggle to acquire goods I think of as basic&quot; and &quot;It's amazing that even middle class people here are able to afford goods I think of as mind-bogglingly luxurious&quot; (probably land and people?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T14:40:59-07:00","id":1414470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1413503-what-is-life-like-for-a-mortal-raised-in-yu-shan-as-a-sidereal-agent?p=1414454#post1414454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thought I had is that the prices of different goods can vary dramatically. The amount of silver/year it takes to hire a full-time servant in Yu-Shan is probably a lot higher than in Creation, so I'd expect a rich person in Creation to have many more servants and less jewelry than a rich person in Yu-Shan. I could imagine someone from Yu-Shan visiting Creation thinking, simultaneously &amp;quot;it's amazing that even the richest people here struggle to acquire goods I think of as basic&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;It's amazing that even middle class people here are able to afford goods I think of as mind-bogglingly luxurious&amp;quot; (probably land and people?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Specifically, anything actually valuable in Yu-Shan isn't acquirable with mortal resources. I believe you added 2 or 3 dots to the cost of things if you were paying with silver or Jade and not Heavenly Currency (which was backed by the UCS and made of ambrosia). At least in 1E. Dunno about 2E or 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader","name":"Scrollreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26421_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-19T01:13:15-07:00","id":1414523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1413503-what-is-life-like-for-a-mortal-raised-in-yu-shan-as-a-sidereal-agent?p=1414118#post1414118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never been a fan of the 'wisdom of the ancients' trope. If they were that smart and powerful, where were their steam engines and antibiotics?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It become a trope for a reason, our ancestors did manage to lose some pretty useful knowledge sometimes. I mean, by now we have managed to figure most of it back out in the current modern age but for awhile it was lost and that is where the trope came from. And if nothing else looking back over their work might give people ideas on how to take some old ideas and run with them in new ways like how people looked into leeches and realized you could make an anticoagulant out of things in their spit that is useful in cases were patients are allergic to more commonly used blood clot fighting medicine. Yeah that isn't a situation that will come up super often but the people who it does come up for are pretty damn glad modern science decided to take a look at how our ancestors were obsessed with treating everything by letting parasites bite them and suck out their blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}